From 475aad87c2e719ad4b2121ec335fc0feba3b07a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 03:12:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] aurora: end each frame at its display copy in worker mode

The display-copy flag was raised by the copy observer on the FIFO worker, and
the main thread presented at its next GX write. By then the worker had often
run on into the next frame's first draws - Wind Waker draws the sky and sea
first - and recorded them into the frame being presented; the next frame then
began without them. The title showed its logo and island over a black sky in
4-14 of 310 captured frames in worker mode and in none with the worker off.

The frontend can now stop a FIFO parse right after a display copy
(set_stop_at_display_copy), leaving the rest buffered. In worker mode the worker
then leaves the recording lock and waits until the main thread has presented;
the main thread presents at its next GX write or inside a drain that is waiting
on the worker, exactly once per stop. After: 0 black frames in three worker runs
and one synchronous run, all with the same 12,269,794 submitted draws. New
frontend test: a flush stops after GXCopyDisp and the next flush resumes.
